      "message": "[Jetski Generated Review]\n\nOverall, this is a valuable cleanup to eliminate reserved double-underscore macros (`__CROS_EC_...`) and standardize header guards across the repository to `PLATFORM_EC_\u003cPATH\u003e_\u003cFILE\u003e_H_`.\n\nHere is a summary of findings to address before landing:\n\n1. **`third_party/boringssl/include/curve25519.h`**: Inadvertently modified via the symlink `include/curve25519.h`. `util/fix_header_guards.py` should be updated to skip symlinks or check resolved paths against excluded directories, and the change to `curve25519.h` should be reverted.\n2. **Script idempotency \u0026 Zephyr shim headers**: Running `util/fix_header_guards.py --use-c-comments --prefix\u003dPLATFORM_EC_ .` on a clean tree is not currently idempotent (modifies 17 files):\n   - It moves `#ifndef` above the `#error` inclusion checks in `zephyr_host_command.h`, `zephyr_hooks_shim.h`, `zephyr_gpio_signal.h`, `zephyr_mkbp_event.h`, and `zephyr_shim.h`. This prematurely defines the macro and causes the `#error` condition to always trigger during Zephyr compilation (the cause of earlier tryjob failures).\n   - It duplicates guards on `ec_commands.h`, `ec_cmd_api.h`, `panic_defs.h`, and `cros_ec_dev.h` because it does not recognize `#if !defined(...) \u0026\u0026 !defined(...)`.\n3. **Continuation comment formatting**: `build_endif_lines()` uses `\\t*/`, which conflicts with `cros format` (`clang-format`), which formats wrapped block comments with 8 spaces (`        */`), leading to formatting churn.\n4. **`util/make_linux_ec_commands_h.sh`**: Dual sed replacements produce duplicate `#if !defined` checks and export an internal `TODO(b/510249930)` comment into the upstream kernel header.\n\nSee inline comments for specific line references and suggestions.",
